# Testing and data quality

## Where tests run

Phase 3 data-quality checks run on Databricks: Delta `NOT NULL` and `CHECK` constraints, plus the reconciliation prints in the notebook. A printed warning does not fail the job. A constraint reject does. Pytest on `data/sample/` (`USE_SAMPLE=1`) is not the Phase 3 definition of done. That local check stays with R46 (S6, Phase 6, Phase 7). Do not add `src/tests/` as a Phase 3 deliverable.

When a later phase adds pytest, the framework is pytest, the default input is `data/sample/`, and tests live in `src/tests/`. The notebook prints the same checks the test will call.

## Required checks

Every Gold load test covers all of the following. `gold.etl_audit` stores only the ten row-count columns: `audit_id`, `run_id`, `layer`, `target_table`, `source_name`, `rows_read`, `rows_loaded`, `rows_rejected`, `rows_unknown_fk`, `loaded_at`. Other warnings are DQ checks printed by the notebook. Do not add them as audit columns.

1. Row reconciliation for the same run: `rows_read = rows_loaded + rows_dropped_by_dedup + rows_rejected`. `rows_dropped_by_dedup` is printed in the notebook, not stored. `rows_rejected` counts rows dropped entirely. A value set to null while the row is still written is a printed DQ warning, not a rejected row.
2. `SUM(price)` on the source order items equals `SUM(price)` on `gold.fact_order_item` for the same run (rejected rows excluded on both sides). Print the totals. Do not store them on `gold.etl_audit`.
3. No orphan foreign keys from facts to dimensions. Unknown keys are `-1`, and `-1` exists.
4. Unique grain: `fact_order_item` (`order_id`, `order_item_id`), `fact_order` (`order_id`), `fact_seller_monthly` (seller, month).
5. NULL rate of each non-key measure stays inside the threshold documented in DESIGN. If DESIGN has no threshold yet, assert the rate and print it; do not invent a pass limit.

Also add Delta `NOT NULL` and `CHECK` constraints on Gold grain keys and on flags that must be 0 or 1.

## Done means executed

Do not say tests passed, a pipeline is done, or a metric has a value unless you ran the command in this session and the report quotes the real output (pass count, failure text, or printed totals). If pytest is not installed or no test file exists yet, say so. See `11-commands-env` for how to run commands.

Sample refresh is not a test. Run `python src/notebooks/00_verify_and_sample.py` only to rebuild `data/sample/` (`04-data-integrity`). DQ assertions belong in pytest, not in that script.
